# Dryas Workflow (Codex)
Process rules for coding sessions on this machine. Full reference: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-workflow.md` (local notes, if present: `~/.dryas/docs/dryas-local.md`).

## Always
- Brainstorm first: before new work, get the user's approval of a design (`$dryas:brainstorm`; design: `$dryas:lens`).
- Reverse-engineering work (how software you don't have the source for does something): use REA; brainstorm says when it recommends it, the user can decline.
- Multi-step work runs in its own git worktree (`$dryas:worktree`); merge after review and verification (`$dryas:verify`).
- One agent per worktree: never run two sessions in the same worktree. Parallel loops each get their own worktree and branch.
- Plans are files: `.orchestrate/PLAN.md` in the worktree, sections `## Task N:` with Goal, Scope (globs), Done and Failing test first. Never commit `.orchestrate/`.
- Test first; report only passes you saw.
- Review before merge: spec compliance, then code quality (`$dryas:wreview`).
- Commit after review as Conventional Commits; ask before any push.
- Do what was asked, nothing more. Read a file before editing it. Never commit secrets or `.env` files.

## Skills
`$dryas:orchestrate` (multi-step tasks), `$dryas:wplan` (write a plan), `$dryas:wreview` (two-stage review), `$dryas:commit` (Jev-gated commit), `$dryas:tune` (weekly Jev calibration), `$dryas:retro` (lessons from a finished task).
<!-- pstack-picks -->
`$dryas:interrogate` (gated two-model review), `$dryas:benchmark-checklist` (vet a measured performance number). Shared references: `{{CD}}/pstack/`.
<!-- /pstack-picks -->

## Jev and Dryas memory (MCP server `jev`; `ruflo` only with the Ruflo extra)
- Jev answers narrow typed questions (`jev_judge`) and never writes code or plans. Below threshold, escalated or unavailable: you decide, and log any disagreement with `log_override`.
- Start a task on a cheaper model; move up when it fails and log each step with `log_escalation` (task, reason, decided_by, from_model, to_model).
- Dryas memory: `memory_search` before a task, `memory_store` after success; namespace = the main repo's folder name.
- Hooks enforce the scope lock (with `.orchestrate/active.json` present, edits outside the active tasks' Scope are denied), the Jev gate on risky commands, and a Jev route hint per prompt.
- Windows PowerShell: put `& ` before a command that starts with a quoted path.

## Not available in Codex
Context-window warnings, compaction handoff, `$handoff` and the memory hooks other than session start run only in Claude Code.
